description:
Be part of this community restoration project by helping to plant 2000 native seedlings. Spades and gloves will be supplied but please bring wet weather gear / sun hat and a drink of water.&nbsp;A free barbecue will be provided after planting. &nbsp;
Park in the car park by the Holiday Park entrance. There is a short walk to the planting site across sloping / uneven ground. Suitable for adults and children, but all children must be actively supervised.
In the event of heavy rain, this event will be postponed to Sunday 14th June.

Francesca Brugnoli has documented the work of Painga Project, a charity working to provide vision and hearing testing for tamariki at local schools. &nbsp;
Her photography exhibition (part of the Auckland Festival of Photography) shows the young children of Onepoto Primary School getting tested and the joy of receiving their first glasses.
It runs from May 29th to June 14th 2026 at Devonport Library. The evening event on June 7th at 6pm is a talk by the co-founder of the Painga Project and a celebration of the exhibition.
